messages.reasoning_content:
The plan is to patch the Deployment `app` in namespace `default`.

The problematic Pod was using an invalid command: `nginx -g not_a_valid_directive on;`.
The Deployment `app` needs its container command updated to a valid one, which for `nginx:1.31.5` should simply be `["nginx"]` or `["nginx", "-g", "daemon off;"]`. I will use `["nginx"]` as the simplest valid command to ensure the service starts.

The patch needs to target the `spec.template.spec.containers` array within the Deployment `app`.

The patch structure will be:
```json
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "command": ["nginx"]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```
I need to use the `kubectl patch` command with `--type=strategic`.

After patching, I must wait for the Deployment to roll out and the Pods to come back to a healthy state (Ready replicas matching desired replicas).

